{"id": "en_blackout_city_p1", "total": 72.93, "segments": [{"text": "If the city grid fails completely, do not light a single candle inside your room.", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.0}, {"text": "Mark stands inside a tall office building as grid power drops without any warning.", "start": 4.76, "end": 8.3}, {"text": "The total dark hits fast, giving Mark exactly 48 hours to survive this blackout.", "start": 8.78, "end": 12.94}, {"text": "Panic spreads outside on dark streets, but Mark stays focused and walks to shelter now.", "start": 13.48, "end": 17.34}, {"text": "He moves fast and decides to enter shelter before pitch darkness covers everything.", "start": 17.84, "end": 21.62}, {"text": "One. Mark stores water early by filling all containers and the bathtub right now.", "start": 22.452, "end": 26.14}, {"text": "Filling containers and the bathtub while taps work secures his life water.", "start": 26.14, "end": 30.0}, {"text": "Two. Mark uses flashlights only because candles cause terrible fires during blackouts.", "start": 30.879, "end": 35.08}, {"text": "Bright battery light protects his shelter without creating open fire hazards tonight.", "start": 35.58, "end": 39.12}, {"text": "Three. Mark keeps the fridge closed tight so food stays safe for 4 hours.", "start": 40.175, "end": 43.6}, {"text": "A full freezer left closed keeps food safe for about 48 hours.", "start": 44.08, "end": 47.12}, {"text": "He never runs a generator, grill, or camp stove indoors because carbon monoxide kills silently.", "start": 47.74, "end": 52.54}, {"text": "Safe inside the tall office building, Mark prepares for the dark night.", "start": 53.2, "end": 56.38}, {"text": "He followed every safety rule and locked down his blackout shelter securely.", "start": 56.92, "end": 60.12}, {"text": "It was the perfect plan, but Mark faces one dangerous problem in the dark building.", "start": 60.56, "end": 64.68}, {"text": "Someone lit a camp stove downstairs, filling the enclosed building with silent c